=====================================================================================
🔹 What is the Linux environment?
=====================================================================================
A Linux environment is a set of variables and settings that are available to
a running process (shell, script, service, command).


These variables control:
- Where commands are found
- How programs behave
- Credentials, tokens, locale, timezone, etc.


=====================================================================================
🔹 Environment variables
=====================================================================================
Environment variables are key=value pairs.

Example
PATH=/usr/bin:/bin
HOME=/home/rahul
USER=rahul

=====================================================================================
🔹 View environment variables
=====================================================================================
env
(or)
printenv


Specific variable:
echo $PATH

=====================================================================================
🔹 Create an environment variable
=====================================================================================
For current shell
MYVAR=hello

Export it (available to child processes)
export MYVAR=hello

=====================================================================================
🔹 Variable scope (VERY important)
=====================================================================================
| Type                | Visible where?          | Lifetime          |
| ------------------- | ----------------------- | ----------------- |
| Shell variable      | Current shell only      | Until shell exits |
| Exported variable   | Shell + child processes | Until shell exits |
| Persistent variable | All future shells       | Until removed     |


=====================================================================================
🔹 Temporary environment for one command
=====================================================================================
MYVAR=hello mycommand


✔ Exists only while mycommand runs
✔ Does not affect your shell

=====================================================================================
🔹 Persistent environment variables
=====================================================================================
User-level
--------------------------
Files:
--------------------------
~/.bashrc

~/.profile

~/.zshrc

Example:

export JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-17

--------------------------
System-wide
--------------------------
Files:

/etc/environment

/etc/profile

/etc/profile.d/*.sh

=====================================================================================
🔹 Common important Linux environment variables
=====================================================================================
| Variable    | Purpose                    |
| ----------- | -------------------------- |
| PATH        | Where shell finds commands |
| HOME        | User home directory        |
| USER        | Current user               |
| SHELL       | Default shell              |
| PWD         | Current directory          |
| LANG / LC_* | Locale                     |
| EDITOR      | Default editor             |


=====================================================================================
🔹 Environment vs Shell config
=====================================================================================

| File               | Purpose                  |
| ------------------ | ------------------------ |
| `.bashrc`          | Interactive shell config |
| `.profile`         | Login shell              |
| `/etc/environment` | Global env vars          |
| systemd unit       | Service env              |


=====================================================================================
🔹 Environment in automation
=====================================================================================
systemd

❌ Does NOT read .bashrc
✔ Use:

Environment="VAR=value"

cron

❌ Minimal environment
✔ Define PATH explicitly

=====================================================================================
🔹 Why environment matters
=====================================================================================

“Command works in terminal but fails in cron/systemd”

Wrong PATH

Missing credentials

Wrong locale or timezone

🧠 Simple mental model

Environment = configuration backpack carried by every process
